Subject: [PATCH] mode: pad raw lines to 16 bytes (qcom-camss VFE alignment)

libmegapixels assumes raw Bayer lines are padded to 8-byte alignment, but
the Qualcomm CAMSS VFE (SDM845/fajita, verified via VIDIOC_G_FMT) pads
bytesperline to 16: 2592px @10bpp -> 3248 (not 3240), 4656px -> 5824 (not
5820). The mismatch trips Megapixels' capture-buffer size assert and would
skew every stride computation (GL debayer padding ratio, repacking, DNG).

Device-scoped workaround for fajita. The proper upstream fix is to stop
recomputing entirely: pipeline.c already records the driver's true
bytesperline in mode->stride — consumers should use it.

--- a/src/mode.c
+++ b/src/mode.c
@@ -329,12 +329,12 @@ libmegapixels_mode_width_to_padding(int index, uint32_t width)
 	if (mode_lut[index].bpp == 8) {
 		return 0;
 	}
 	uint64_t bytes_per_width = libmegapixels_mode_width_to_bytes(index, width);
-	uint64_t remainder = bytes_per_width % 8;
+	uint64_t remainder = bytes_per_width % 16;
 	if (remainder == 0)
 		return remainder;

-	return 8 - remainder;
+	return 16 - remainder;
 }

 uint32_t
